Seven model pages under **Data Models**, and a corrected group-weight table in `docs/dev/extending.md`.

Three of the pages carry a measured warning rather than a preference. [AI Agent Subagent](../docs/models/aiagentsubagent.md) records that a name and a description decide whether a specialist is called at all, and that the failure is silence: in one measured test, three of four wordings never called the tool in ten runs each. The same page records that sending the question of the user alongside the task broke the system on every run, because the added text matched a rule in the prompt of the specialist. [AI Skill](../docs/models/aiskill.md) records that a rule delivered as a tool result did not hold where the same rule held in a system prompt.

A user guide page for Git-sourced tools: the repository layout, the required root `__init__.py`, what each sync does to a record, and why the trust boundary is the one Nautobot already draws for Git-sourced Jobs.
